 3 load_config -> owned seam (ensures.py maybe_emit_pending_hint and project_ensures.py _effective_project now call config.compose_config(); push.py _push_mode now calls new config.resolve_push_mode(root), which reads sync.push LIVE per call via load_config(root).sync.push wrapping normalize_push_mode, ConfigError -> \"always\" -- preserves the import_ndjson REBAR_SYNC_PUSH defer coupling). git_fetch stall knobs (FLOOR/WINDOW/ATTEMPTS) -> config.resolve_stall_abort_limits/resolve_stall_attempts (git_fetch._positive_int removed). janitor 5x REBAR_GATE_* plus the dynamic os.environ.get at L73 -> config.resolve_janitor_tunables(defaults, root); JanitorConfig.from_env now RECEIVES resolved values (janitor._int_pref/_read_snapshot_table removed). repo_snapshot.store_root -> config.resolve_gate_tmpdir. env_identity.override_enabled -> config.resolve_allow_env_reidentify. lock.write_path_retries -> config.resolve_lock_retries(default, max) (see advisory below).\n\nOWNED-IN-PLACE markers (5 lines, the cap): hlc.py L61 REBAR_HLC (subsystem-kill-switch), L71 REBAR_HLC_NOW (test-only-clock-injection); import_ndjson.py L216/L217/L395 REBAR_SYNC_PUSH (subprocess-env-control). No other listed source file carries a marker.\n\nconfig.py resolvers added: resolve_push_mode (live per call, in config.py per the plan). The remaining resolvers (resolve_stall_abort_limits, resolve_stall_attempts, resolve_gate_tmpdir, resolve_allow_env_reidentify, resolve_lock_retries, resolve_janitor_tunables plus helpers _positive_int/_snapshot_table/_snapshot_int) live in rebar._config_sources (also an OWNED composition-root basename; this keeps config.py under the 800 LOC hard cap -- config.py is 721 LOC) and are re-exported from rebar.config, so callers use rebar.config.resolve_*. Env-name literals are inlined in these owned resolvers so gen_env_registry still documents them; docs/env-vars.md regenerated -- the 11 cut vars now attribute to _config_sources.py, while REBAR_HLC/HLC_NOW/SYNC_PUSH stay attributed to their in-place files.\n\nwrite_path_retries(): per advisory, signature UNCHANGED. It reads the clamped retry count from config.resolve_lock_retries(_WRITE_PATH_RETRIES, _MAX_RETRIES) INTERNALLY, so the event_append.py and txn.py call sites that pass retries=write_path_retries() are untouched.\n\nExtra marker (outside the 10 cut files): SyncConfig.push in _config_schema.py got a '# read-via: config.py resolve_push_mode()' marker to satisfy the sibling check_config_reads.py gate, because the .sync.push attribute-read site moved out of push.py into the config resolver. This is the established convention (cf. 'readonly ... # read-via: config.py mcp_readonly()') and _config_schema.py is NOT one of the 10 store/snapshot/io files, so the exactly-5-marker cap there is unaffected.\n\nSemantics preserved: env>config>default for the [snapshot] janitor knobs; env>default for the stall knobs; [0, _MAX_RETRIES] clamp for REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES; live-per-call for push mode.\n\nTest consumers: no tests/unit files needed edits. Every listed consumer injects via monkeypatch.setenv or explicit JanitorConfig(...) kwargs, and the relocated reads still read the same env vars (now from the owned config seam), so no injection path changed -- per the ticket's \"only touch tests whose injection path actually changed\".\n\nValidation: (1) check_config_ownership.py exit 0, no output. (2) zero _store/_snapshot/_io rows remain in LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS. (3) make lint + make typecheck clean; complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0; module sizes under 800. (4) behavioral suites 578 passed / 9 skipped; one unrelated REPO_ROOT-leak ERROR from a foreign '.rp3_full.txt' artifact (another slice), which passes clean in isolation.","timestamp":1787108744015836001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion evidence (Gerrit 1888, LLM-Review+1 AND Verified+1, CI SUCCESS run 32212210867):\n- All 15 store/snapshot/io reads cut-to-seam through owned config.py/_config_sources.py resolvers; 3 owned-in-place reads = 5 # read-via: marked lines confined to _store/hlc.py(2)+_io/import_ndjson.py(3). push mode cut to LIVE-per-call config.resolve_push_mode (not compose-once).\n- 18 LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS rows removed; scripts/check_config_ownership.py exits 0 with no path-glob exception. Held-out oracle tests/scripts/test_store_snapshot_io_seam_clean_heldout.py GREEN (gate-clean + zero rows + marker-total==5/per-file placement); teeth confirmed (marker-removal mutant -> RED).\n- Regression suites GREEN incl. the REBAR_SYNC_PUSH import-defer coupling oracle (tests/unit/test_c3b_push_defer_coupling_heldout.py, server-side push-count observation; compose-once mutant -> RED). 529 targeted pass; 3 env-only shared-store collision errors pass clean in isolation.\n- Operation-snapshot fingerprints / provider-neutral outcomes UNCHANGED (delta = none): the cut relocates ownership only; resolvers read the SAME env vars live, so no observable behavior or fingerprint changes.","timestamp":1787112080907868001}],"created_at":1787095110680331001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"3cde6b95-c41f-4461-88fb-3bcbf385040b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ff2a-9b3c-f5fd-41a2"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nSlice C1 (29a9-3cf7-3ded-42d8) recorded 18 below-seam ambient config/credential reads in the store/snapshot/io subsystem (_store, _snapshot, _io) as `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` rows in `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py`. RP-04 is not complete while these sit below the seams enforced by `scripts/check_config_ownership.py`. Parent: 075b-1479-dcb7-40ab.\n\nThe 18 flagged reads: 3 `load_config()` (_store/ensures.py:245, _store/project_ensures.py:69, _store/push.py:63); env reads REBAR_SNAPSHOT_STALL_{ATTEMPTS,WINDOW_SECONDS,FLOOR_BYTES_PER_SEC} (git_fetch.py), REBAR_GATE_{FREE_WATERMARK_BYTES,GRACE_SECONDS,JANITOR_INTERVAL_SECONDS,MAX_AGE_SECONDS,REVERIFY_SECONDS} + a dynamic os.environ.get (janitor.py L73), REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR (repo_snapshot.py), REBAR_ALLOW_ENV_REIDENTIFY (env_identity.py), REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES (lock.py), REBAR_HLC + REBAR_HLC_NOW (hlc.py), REBAR_SYNC_PUSH (import_ndjson.py L216/217/395).\n\nAffected SOURCE files: the 10 above plus `src/rebar/config.py` (adds/reuses owned resolvers) and `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py` (removes the 18 rows).\n\nAffected TEST consumers (updated in-scope — they set the cut env vars directly and drive the affected helpers): `tests/unit/test_snapshot_janitor.py`, `test_snapshot_fetch_stall_abort_12e4.py`, `test_network_fetch_stall_abort_851e.py`, `test_repo_snapshot.py`, `test_snapshot_cache.py`, `test_snapshot_blobless_747f.py`, `test_snapshot_docs.py`, `test_lock_retry_zebrafish.py`, and any test setting `REBAR_ALLOW_ENV_REIDENTIFY` driving `_store/env_identity.py`.\n\n## Outcome\nEach of the 18 reads is dispositioned by the decision rule into exactly one treatment and its `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` row removed. `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` reports zero findings for these paths, no path-glob exception. Regression suites (below) stay green, including the REBAR_SYNC_PUSH import-defer coupling. Redacted operation-snapshot fingerprints / provider-neutral outcomes unchanged except recorded deltas (comment on this ticket).\n\n## Decision rule\n- **(a) CUT-TO-SEAM (default; majority).** A read whose value is composed config is CUT: routed through an owned `config.py` resolver instead of ambient `os.environ`/`load_config` below the seam; the ambient read no longer exists. Below-seam helper signatures change to RECEIVE the value, so the `tests/unit` consumers inject via the new signature/typed config and run in the regression suite. **Preserve resolution timing:** a read resolved live per operation is cut to a resolver that itself reads live per call (see push.py coupling), NOT composed once and threaded — otherwise a mid-operation override is silently lost.\n- **(b) OWNED-IN-PLACE via `# read-via:` marker (bounded allowlist ONLY).** A read that is NOT composed config — genuine test-only injection, subsystem kill-switch, or subprocess/protocol env-control — stays with a `# read-via:` marker naming the category. CAPPED at the 3 enumerated logical reads below; the gate flags each accessed LINE separately, so those 3 reads = exactly **5 marked lines**. No other listed read may be marked.\n\n### Owned-in-place allowlist (3 reads = 5 marked lines — the cap)\n1. `_store/hlc.py` L61 `REBAR_HLC` — subsystem kill-switch (`REBAR_HLC=0` reverts HLC to raw `physical_now()`). 1 line.\n2. `_store/hlc.py` L71 `REBAR_HLC_NOW` — test-only injection of the physical clock source. 1 line.\n3. `_io/import_ndjson.py` L216/L217/L395 `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH` — subprocess/protocol env-control: L216 reads prior value, L217 sets `=off` (defer per-event push during bulk import), L395 restores. Not composed config. 3 lines.\n\nAll 15 other reads are treatment (a).\n\n## The push.py / import_ndjson coupling (must stay correct)\n`push.py:63` resolves `sync.push` **live per push**, and `import_ndjson` sets `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=off` in the process env precisely so those live reads defer per-event pushes during a bulk import, then restores and does one final push. Cutting push.py to a value composed once at the seam would stop it observing that mutation and break import push-deferral. Resolution: cut push.py:63 to an owned `config.py` resolver `resolve_push_mode(root)` that resolves **live per call** (env>config>`always` default, wrapping `normalize_push_mode`); push.py's `_push_mode` keeps its `current_push_mode()` startup-binding precedence then calls the live resolver. import_ndjson's `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH` env-control stays owned-in-place (b) and continues to drive that live resolver. Same live-per-call rule applies to any other live-resolved read among the cuts.\n\n## Plan\n1. Add/confirm owned `config.py` resolvers (reuse `compose_config()`; add `resolve_push_mode(root)` live resolver; add narrow typed resolvers where cleaner). Cut the 15 composed-config reads to route through them, changing below-seam helper signatures to RECEIVE the value. Preserve exact semantics (env>config>default for `[snapshot]` knobs; clamping for `REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES`; live-per-call for push mode).\n2. Update the affected `tests/unit` consumers to inject via the new signature/typed config; keep their assertions.\n3. Mark the 3 owned-in-place reads (5 lines) with `# read-via:` markers naming the category; no other markers.\n4. Remove the 18 rows from `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS`.\n5. Run `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` and the regression set; keep green.\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\nHeld-out `tests/scripts/test_store_snapshot_io_seam_clean_heldout.py` asserts: (i) `check_config_ownership.check(REPO_ROOT)` returns no finding containing any listed source path; (ii) `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` has zero entries whose `path` is a listed source file; (iii) `# read-via:` markers across the listed source files total exactly 5, confined to `_store/hlc.py` (2) and `_io/import_ndjson.py` (3) — every other listed file has 0 — so blanket-marking cannot substitute for cutting. RED now.\nCoupling regression (held-out): a bulk `import_ndjson` run with N interior writes and `sync.push=always` performs exactly ONE push (proving the cut `resolve_push_mode` still observes the mid-import `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=off` env mutation); RED if push.py is cut to a compose-once value.\nRegression suites kept green: `tests/interfaces/store`, `tests/integration` store/snapshot, AND the affected `tests/unit` suites listed above. Redacted operation-snapshot fingerprints before/after equal except recorded deltas.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nNo stored format changes. Cut-to-seam is routing/threading; the 5 marked lines are inline annotations on 3 non-config env-control reads. Rollback = revert the single change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] No ambient config/credential read, backend reload, or configurable default remains below the seam in the 10 listed source files: each read is cut-to-seam (15) or one of the 3 enumerated owned-in-place reads (5 marked lines) with a `# read-via:` rationale; no other read marked; live-resolved reads (push mode) cut to a live-per-call resolver, not a compose-once value.\n- [x] The 18 `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` rows are removed and `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` passes with no path-glob exception (proven by the held-out test incl. its marker-total==5 / per-file-placement check).\n- [x] The regression suites in Testing pass after the cutover, including the REBAR_SYNC_PUSH import-defer coupling test; operation-snapshot fingerprints / provider-neutral outcomes unchanged except deltas recorded with rationale as a comment on this ticket.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py","reason":"Cut below-seam config/credential read to the approved seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/git_fetch.py","reason":"Cut below-seam config/credential read to the approved seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py","reason":"Cut below-seam config/credential read to the approved seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py","reason":"Cut below-seam config/credential read to the approved seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/ensures.py","reason":"Cut below-seam config/credential read to the approved seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/env_identity.py","reason":"Cut below-seam config/credential read to the approved seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/hlc.py","reason":"Cut below-seam config/credential read to the approved seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/lock.py","reason":"Cut below-seam config/credential read to the approved seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/project_ensures.py","reason":"Cut below-seam config/credential read to the approved seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/push.py","reason":"Cut below-seam config/credential read to the approved seam."},{"path":"scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py","reason":"Remove C3b LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS entries as reads are cut to seam."},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_store_snapshot_io_seam_clean_heldout.py","reason":"Held-out proof: gate clean + zero legacy entries for these files."},{"path":"src/rebar/config.py","reason":"Owned composition-root resolvers (resolve_push_mode + re-exports)."},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_sources.py","reason":"Owned resolvers for the cut store/snapshot/io reads."},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_schema.py","reason":"read-via marker on SyncConfig.push for the sibling reads gate."},{"path":"docs/env-vars.md","reason":"Regenerated env-var registry after relocating reads to owned seams."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_c3b_push_defer_coupling_heldout.py","reason":"Held-out REBAR_SYNC_PUSH import-defer coupling oracle."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","075b-1479-dcb7-40ab"],["relates_to","ff2a-9b3c-f5fd-41a2"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"075b-1479-dcb7-40ab","parent_status_uuid":"916f16df-d2fb-4ca1-8e26-ef3a4dfbc436","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"d074-ab22-e37a-4480","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-04 S7.3.b — store-snapshot-io cutover: route below-seam config reads through seams","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["98b4452e-25bd-43f5-9577-91f77dfe4853","0081e6ed-788d-430f-9731-52e534a89eee","7ba03e33-1d09-4c47-ae2c-ca5fa6501871","aa77a1c9-56c4-4b04-baae-d864bf2f7e91","e74c5a86-89ba-46d2-b7a6-053987683831","6fc6762d-5296-4a55-82d2-88c6c3f599c2","b651e854-80f6-4cb2-9521-972c610d8c05","013d2810-79a0-45a6-9835-402127434503","3cde6b95-c41f-4461-88fb-3bcbf385040b","bada4205-5dc9-4515-84cf-7080fa73f7f9","f01b4a52-624e-45b1-8a98-d223d7322b2b","d3cfa491-dd1a-4962-8dac-eae3f3a00f3c","19b75f8f-08a1-4e07-8285-2599ab0ef6b6","916f16df-d2fb-4ca1-8e26-ef3a4dfbc436","aa5c771d-5df1-450e-8e68-f6e9f77e96a4"]},"env_